---@field performHPO? aws.personalize.Boolean Whether to perform hyperparameter optimization (HPO) on the specified or selected recipe. The default is false.
---@field performAutoML? aws.personalize.PerformAutoML We don't recommend enabling automated machine learning. Instead, match your use case to the available Amazon Personalize recipes. For more information, see Choosing a recipe. Whether to perform automated machine learning (AutoML). The default is false. For this case, you must specify recipeArn. When set to true, Amazon Personalize analyzes your training data and selects the optimal USER_PERSONALIZ...
---@field performAutoTraining? aws.personalize.PerformAutoTraining Whether the solution uses automatic training to create new solution versions (trained models). The default is True and the solution automatically creates new solution versions every 7 days. You can change the training frequency by specifying a schedulingExpression in the AutoTrainingConfig as part of solution configuration. For more information about automatic training, see Configuring automatic t...
---@field performIncrementalUpdate? aws.personalize.PerformIncrementalUpdate Whether to perform incremental training updates on your model. When enabled, this allows the model to learn from new data more frequently without requiring full retraining, which enables near real-time personalization. This parameter is supported only for solutions that use the semantic-similarity recipe.
---@field recipeArn? aws.personalize.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the recipe to use for model training. This is required when performAutoML is false. For information about different Amazon Personalize recipes and their ARNs, see Choosing a recipe.
---@field datasetGroupArn aws.personalize.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the dataset group that provides the training data.
---@field eventType? aws.personalize.EventType When your have multiple event types (using an EVENT_TYPE schema field), this parameter specifies which event type (for example, 'click' or 'like') is used for training the model.
---@field solutionConfig? aws.personalize.SolutionConfig The configuration properties for the solution. When performAutoML is set to true, Amazon Personalize only evaluates the autoMLConfig section of the solution configuration.
---@field tags? aws.personalize.Tags A list of tags to apply to the solution.

---@class aws.personalize.CreateSolutionResponse
---@field solutionArn? aws.personalize.Arn The ARN of the solution.

---@class aws.personalize.CreateSolutionVersionRequest
---@field name? aws.personalize.Name The name of the solution version.
---@field solutionArn aws.personalize.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the solution containing the training configuration information.
---@field trainingMode? aws.personalize.TrainingMode|string The scope of training to be performed when creating the solution version. The default is FULL. This creates a completely new model based on the entirety of the training data from the datasets in your dataset group.
---@field tags? aws.personalize.Tags A list of tags to apply to the solution version.

---@class aws.personalize.CreateSolutionVersionResponse
---@field solutionVersionArn? aws.personalize.Arn The ARN of the new solution version.

